# ==========================================================================
# PATIENT DATA AND SECRETS -- these two blocks are the ones that matter
# ==========================================================================
#
# Uploaded laboratory reports are PHI. `UPLOAD_ROOT` defaults to
# `backend/storage/uploads` and is resolved against the backend directory
# (see backend/src/config/env.js), but it is configurable, so the common
# names are all excluded rather than just the default. A report that reaches
# a commit is in every clone and every backup for good.
storage/
uploads/
**/storage/uploads/

# Report bytes wherever they land, scoped to the directories they land in.
# NOT a blanket `*.pdf` / `*.png`: `datasets/population/reference/` holds the
# two published NCHS documents Module 31's tables were cross-checked against,
# and those are provenance, not patient data.
**/uploads/**
**/storage/**

# Real credentials. `.env.example` is committed on purpose -- it documents
# which variables exist without carrying a single value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ==========================================================================
# Dependencies and build products
# ==========================================================================
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Jest / pytest scratch
junit*.xml
*.junit.xml

# ==========================================================================
# Editor and OS noise
# ==========================================================================
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ==========================================================================
# DELIBERATELY COMMITTED, despite being large or generated
# ==========================================================================
#
# ml/artifacts/*.joblib  (~35 MB total)
#     The three trained models. They are the artifacts the service LOADS --
#     nothing retrains at runtime -- and their metrics JSON is the source of
#     every performance figure a clinician is shown. Excluding them would
#     leave a clone unable to make a prediction.
#
# datasets/population/raw/*.xpt  (~14 MB total)
#     The NHANES microdata the percentile tables were built from. These are
#     downloadable, and PROVENANCE.md records a SHA-256 for each, so they
#     could be re-fetched -- but an independent auditor reproduced all seven
#     tables from THESE files, and keeping them makes that reproducible
#     without depending on a CDC URL still resolving years from now.
#     Verifiable provenance is a core rule of this project, not a nicety.
#
# datasets/*/*.csv
#     The three real ML training datasets, for the same reason.
#
# Nothing above is ignored. This block exists so the decision is recorded
# rather than rediscovered.
